    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class, `AcceptanceTest`, is green, and everything compiles.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule so that creating an owner whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**, following the exact pattern of the existing telephone/household duplicate rules.\n\nChanges, each in its natural place:\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException`** (new) \u2014 a small domain exception mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `findOwnersByEmail(String)`, which looks up owners by email case-insensitively (mirroring the existing `findOwnersInSameHousehold` stream approach; robust even if any stored email isn't already normalized). The persistence query lives in the service layer, not the controller.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added the duplicate-email guard right after the telephone check. It skips the check when no email was supplied (email is optional), since the emails are already normalized/lower-cased upstream by `EmailNormalizer`.\n\n4. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a handler mapping `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` to 409 with `errors: [\"email\"]`, consistent with the sibling handlers.\n\nNo existing implementations of `ClinicService` other than `ClinicServiceImpl` exist, so the interface addition was safe.",
